Table full name: TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0.TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0.SOMATIC_MUTATION
Column name: normal_bam_uuid Type: TEXT Description: Unique GDC identifier for the underlying normal bam file
Column name: HGVSp_Short Type: TEXT Description: Same as the HGVSp column, but using 1-letter amino-acid codes
Column name: ExAC_AF_NFE Type: TEXT Description: Non-Finnish European Allele Frequency from ExAC
Column name: Amino_acids Type: TEXT Description: Amino acid substitution caused by the mutation. Only given if the variation affects the protein-coding sequence
Column name: aliquot_barcode_tumor Type: TEXT Description: TCGA aliquot barcode for the tumor, eg TCGA-12-1089-01A-01D-0517-01
Column name: fileName Type: TEXT Description: |-delimited list of name of underlying MAF file
Column name: Tumor_Sample_UUID Type: TEXT Description: Unique GDC identifier for tumor aliquot (10189 unique)
Column name: EUR_MAF Type: FLOAT Description: Non-reference allele and frequency of existing variant in 1000 Genomes combined European population
Column name: Sequencer Type: TEXT Description: Instrument used to produce primary sequence data
Column name: HGVSc Type: TEXT Description: The coding sequence of the variant in HGVS recommended format
Column name: CONTEXT Type: TEXT Description: The reference allele per VCF specs, and its five flanking base pairs
Column name: src_vcf_id Type: TEXT Description: |-delimited list of GDC VCF file identifiers
Column name: tumor_bam_uuid Type: TEXT Description: Unique GDC identifier for the underlying bam file
Column name: ExAC_AF Type: TEXT Description: Global Allele Frequency from   ExAC
Column name: ExAC_AF_AFR Type: TEXT Description: African/African American Allele Frequency from ExAC
Column name: Start_Position Type: NUMBER Description: Lowest numeric position of the reported variant on the genomic reference sequence. Mutation start coordinate
Column name: UNIPARC Type: TEXT Description: UniParc identifier of protein product
Column name: TRANSCRIPT_STRAND Type: NUMBER Description: The DNA strand (1 or -1) on which the transcript/feature lies
Column name: t_depth Type: TEXT Description: Read depth across this locus in tumor BAM
Column name: SOMATIC Type: TEXT Description: Somatic status of each ID reported under Existing_variation (0, 1, or null)
Column name: ExAC_AF_AMR Type: TEXT Description: American Allele Frequency from ExAC
Column name: sample_barcode_tumor Type: TEXT Description: TCGA sample barcode for the tumor, eg TCGA-12-1089-01A. One sample may have multiple sets of CN segmentations corresponding to multiple aliquots; use GROUP BY appropriately in queries
Column name: INTRON Type: TEXT Description: The intron number (out of total number)
Column name: t_ref_count Type: TEXT Description: Read depth supporting the reference allele in tumor BAM
Column name: Chromosome Type: TEXT Description: Chromosome, possible values: chr1-22, and chrX
Column name: PolyPhen Type: TEXT Description: The PolyPhen prediction and/or score
Column name: Tumor_Validation_Allele2 Type: TEXT Description: Secondary data from orthogonal technology. Tumor genotyping (validation) for allele 2
Column name: sample_barcode_normal Type: TEXT Description: TCGA sample barcode for the normal control, eg TCGA-12-1089-01A. One sample may have multiple sets of CN segmentations corresponding to multiple aliquots; use GROUP BY appropriately in queries
Column name: case_id Type: TEXT Description: Unique GDC identifier for the underlying case
Column name: Matched_Norm_Sample_UUID Type: TEXT Description: Unique GDC identifier for normal aliquot (10189 unique)
Column name: RefSeq Type: TEXT Description: RefSeq identifier for this transcript
Column name: Existing_variation Type: TEXT Description: Known identifier of existing variation
Column name: AMR_MAF Type: FLOAT Description: Non-reference allele and frequency of existing variant in 1000 Genomes combined American population
Column name: CDS_position Type: TEXT Description: Relative position of base pair in coding sequence. A - symbol is displayed as the numerator if the variant does not appear in coding sequence
Column name: Variant_Classification Type: TEXT Description: Translational effect of variant allele
Column name: TREMBL Type: TEXT Description: UniProtKB/TrEMBL identifier of protein product
Column name: CANONICAL Type: TEXT Description: A flag (YES) indicating that the VEP-based canonical transcript, the longest translation, was used for this gene. If not, the value is null
Column name: Transcript_ID Type: TEXT Description: Ensembl ID of the transcript affected by the variant
Column name: Tumor_Seq_Allele1 Type: TEXT Description: Primary data genotype for tumor sequencing (discovery) allele 1. A - symbol for a deletion represents a variant. A - symbol for an insertion represents wild-type allele. Novel inserted sequence for insertion does not include flanking reference bases
Column name: Allele Type: TEXT Description: The variant allele used to calculate the consequence
Column name: dbSNP_RS Type: TEXT Description: The rs-IDs from the   dbSNP database, novel if not found in any database used, or null if there is no dbSNP record, but it is found in other databases
Column name: NCBI_Build Type: TEXT Description: The reference genome used for the alignment (GRCh38)
Column name: AFR_MAF Type: FLOAT Description: Non-reference allele and frequency of existing variant in 1000 Genomes combined African population
Column name: HGVSp Type: TEXT Description: The protein sequence of the variant in HGVS recommended format. p.= signifies no change in the protein
Column name: TSL Type: NUMBER Description: Transcript support level, which is based on independent RNA analyses
Column name: Consequence Type: TEXT Description: Consequence type of this variant; sequence ontology terms
Column name: VARIANT_CLASS Type: TEXT Description: Sequence Ontology variant class
Column name: Mutation_Status Type: TEXT Description: An assessment of the mutation as somatic, germline, LOH, post transcriptional modification, unknown, or none. The values allowed in this field are constrained by the value in the Validation_Status field
Column name: CCDS Type: TEXT Description: The  CCDS identifier for this transcript, where applicable
Column name: SYMBOL Type: TEXT Description: Eg TP53, LRP1B, etc (same as Hugo_Symbol field except blank instead of Unknown
Column name: End_Position Type: NUMBER Description: Highest numeric genomic position of the reported variant on the genomic reference sequence. Mutation end coordinate
Column name: AA_MAF Type: TEXT Description: Non-reference allele and frequency of existing variant in NHLBI-ESP African American population
Column name: fileUUID Type: TEXT Description: |-delimited list of unique GDC identifiers for underlying MAF file
Column name: ExAC_AF_SAS Type: TEXT Description: South Asian Allele Frequency from ExAC
Column name: HGNC_ID Type: TEXT Description: Gene identifier from the HUGO Gene Nomenclature Committee if applicable
Column name: callerName Type: TEXT Description: |-delimited list of mutation caller(s) that agreed on this particular call, always in alphabetical order: muse, mutect, somaticsniper, varscan
Column name: FILTER Type: TEXT Description: Copied from input VCF. This includes filters implemented directly by the variant caller and other external software used in the DNA-Seq pipeline. See below for additional details.
Column name: GDC_Validation_Status Type: TEXT Description: GDC implementation of validation checks. See notes section (#5) below for details
Column name: Protein_position Type: TEXT Description: Relative position of affected amino acid in protein. A - symbol is displayed as the numerator if the variant does not appear in coding sequence
Column name: project_short_name Type: TEXT Description: Project name abbreviation; the program name appended with a project name abbreviation; eg. TCGA-OV, etc.
Column name: Codons Type: TEXT Description: The alternative codons with the variant base in upper case
Column name: HGVS_OFFSET Type: NUMBER Description: Indicates by how many bases the HGVS notations for this variant have been shifted
Column name: One_Consequence Type: TEXT Description: The single consequence of the canonical transcript in  sequence ontology terms, eg missense_variant
Column name: BIOTYPE Type: TEXT Description: Biotype of transcript
Column name: Exon_Number Type: TEXT Description: The exon number (out of total number)
Column name: EXON Type: TEXT Description: The exon number (out of total number)
Column name: MC3_Overlap Type: TEXT Description: Indicates whether this region overlaps with an MC3 variant for the same sample pair
Column name: Feature Type: TEXT Description: Stable Ensembl ID of feature (transcript, regulatory, motif)
Column name: SYMBOL_SOURCE Type: TEXT Description: The source of the gene symbol, usually HGNC, rarely blank, other sources include Uniprot_gn, EntrezGene, etc
Column name: SWISSPROT Type: TEXT Description: UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot accession
Column name: Feature_type Type: TEXT Description: Type of feature. Currently one of Transcript, RegulatoryFeature, MotifFeature (or blank)
Column name: ExAC_AF_EAS Type: TEXT Description: East Asian Allele Frequency from ExAC
Column name: t_alt_count Type: TEXT Description: Read depth supporting the variant allele in tumor BAM
Column name: ExAC_AF_FIN Type: TEXT Description: Finnish Allele Frequency from ExAC
Column name: all_effects Type: TEXT Description: A semicolon delimited list of all possible variant effects, sorted by priority ([Symbol,Consequence,HGVSp_Short,Transcript_ID,RefSeq,HGVSc,Impact,Canonical,Sift,PolyPhen,Strand])
Column name: ExAC_AF_OTH Type: TEXT Description: Other Allele Frequency from ExAC
Column name: SIFT Type: TEXT Description: The   SIFT prediction and/or score, with both given as prediction (score)
Column name: Center Type: TEXT Description: One or more genome sequencing center reporting the variant
Column name: dbSNP_Val_Status Type: TEXT Description: The dbSNP validation status is reported as a semicolon-separated list of statuses. The union of all rs-IDs is taken when there are multiple
Column name: ALLELE_NUM Type: TEXT Description: Allele number from input; 0 is reference, 1 is first alternate etc.
Column name: PHENO Type: TEXT Description: Indicates if existing variant is associated with a phenotype, disease or trait (0, 1, or null)
Column name: Tumor_Seq_Allele2 Type: TEXT Description: Primary data genotype for tumor sequencing (discovery) allele 2. A - symbol for a deletion represents a variant. A - symbol for an insertion represents wild-type allele. Novel inserted sequence for insertion does not include flanking reference bases
Column name: PUBMED Type: TEXT Description: Pubmed ID(s) of publications that cite existing variant
Column name: Validation_Method Type: TEXT Description: The assay platforms used for the validation call
Column name: SAS_MAF Type: FLOAT Description: Non-reference allele and frequency of existing variant in 1000 Genomes combined South Asian population
Column name: COSMIC Type: TEXT Description: Overlapping COSMIC variants
Column name: PICK Type: TEXT Description: Indicates if this block of consequence data was picked by VEP's   pick feature (1 or null)
Column name: Entrez_Gene_Id Type: NUMBER Description: Entrez gene ID (an integer). 0 is used for regions that do not correspond to a gene region or Ensembl ID
Column name: Tumor_Validation_Allele1 Type: TEXT Description: Secondary data from orthogonal technology. Tumor genotyping (validation) for allele 1. A - symbol for a deletion represents a variant. A - symbol for an insertion represents wild-type allele. Novel inserted sequence for insertion does not include flanking reference bases
Column name: Gene Type: TEXT Description: The gene symbol. In this table, gene symbol is gene name e.g. ACADVL
Column name: case_barcode Type: TEXT Description: Original TCGA case barcode, eg TCGA-DX-A8BN
Column name: n_depth Type: TEXT Description: Read depth across this locus in normal BAM
Column name: ENSP Type: TEXT Description: The Ensembl protein identifier of the affected transcript
Column name: MINIMISED Type: TEXT Description: Alleles in this variant have been converted to minimal representation before consequence calculation (1 or null)
Column name: EAS_MAF Type: FLOAT Description: Non-reference allele and frequency of existing variant in 1000 Genomes combined East Asian population
Column name: Variant_Type Type: TEXT Description: Type of mutation. TNP (tri-nucleotide polymorphism) is analogous to DNP (di-nucleotide polymorphism) but for three consecutive nucleotides. ONP (oligo-nucleotide polymorphism) is analogous to TNP but for consecutive runs of four or more (SNP, DNP, TNP, ONP, INS, DEL, or Consolidated)
Column name: CLIN_SIG Type: TEXT Description: Clinical significance of variant from dbSNP
Column name: Strand Type: TEXT Description: Either + or - to denote whether read mapped to the sense (+) or anti-sense (-) strand
Column name: Hugo_Symbol Type: TEXT Description: HUGO symbol for the gene (HUGO symbols are always in all caps). Unknown is used for regions that do not correspond to a gene
Column name: Reference_Allele Type: TEXT Description: The plus strand reference allele at this position. Includes the deleted sequence for a deletion or - for an insertion
Column name: DISTANCE Type: NUMBER Description: Shortest distance from the variant to transcript
Column name: GMAF Type: FLOAT Description: Non-reference allele and frequency of existing variant in   1000 Genomes
Column name: cDNA_position Type: TEXT Description: Relative position of base pair in the cDNA sequence as a fraction. A - symbol is displayed as the numerator if the variant does not appear in cDNA
Column name: ExAC_AF_Adj Type: TEXT Description: Adjusted Global Allele Frequency from ExAC
Column name: aliquot_barcode_normal Type: TEXT Description: TCGA aliquot barcode for the normal control, eg TCGA-12-1089-01A-01D-0517-01
Column name: DOMAINS Type: TEXT Description: The source and identifier of any overlapping protein domains
Column name: EA_MAF Type: TEXT Description: Non-reference allele and frequency of existing variant in NHLBI-ESP European American population
Column name: IMPACT Type: TEXT Description: The impact modifier for the consequence type
Column name: GDC_FILTER Type: TEXT Description: GDC filters applied universally across all MAFs
