Table full name: TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0.TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0.COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED_R14
Column name: case_barcode Type: TEXT Description: Original TCGA case barcode, eg TCGA-DX-A8BN
Column name: chromosome Type: TEXT Description: Chromosome, possible values: chr1-22, and chrX
Column name: segment_mean Type: FLOAT Description: Mean CN value for this segment -- the value is base2 log(CN/2), centered at 0.
Column name: sample_gdc_id Type: TEXT Description: Unique GDC identifier for this sample (corresponds to the sample_barcode), eg a1ec9279-c1a6-4e58-97ed-9ec1f36187c5  --  this can be used to access more information from the GDC data portal
Column name: num_probes Type: NUMBER Description: Number of probes in the SNP array used to infer this CN segment
Column name: aliquot_gdc_id Type: TEXT Description: Unique GDC identifier for this aliquot (corresponds to the aliquot_barcode), eg 7fbfdb3e-1fd2-4206-8d2e-7f68e4a15844  --  this can be used to access more information from the GDC data portal
Column name: end_pos Type: NUMBER Description: 1-based end chromosome position of isoform
Column name: sample_barcode Type: TEXT Description: TCGA sample barcode, eg TCGA-12-1089-01A. One sample may have multiple sets of CN segmentations corresponding to multiple aliquots; use GROUP BY appropriately in queries
Column name: start_pos Type: NUMBER Description: 1-based start chromosome position of isoform
Column name: case_gdc_id Type: TEXT Description: Unique GDC identifier for this case (corresponds to the case_barcode).  Can be used to access more information from the GDC data portal like this:   https://portal.gdc.cancer.gov/files/c21b332c-06c6-4403-9032-f91c8f407ba10
Column name: aliquot_barcode Type: TEXT Description: TCGA aliquot barcode, eg TCGA-12-1089-01A-01D-0517-02
Column name: project_short_name Type: TEXT Description: Project name abbreviation; the program name appended with a project name abbreviation; e.g. TCGA-OV, etc.
Column name: file_gdc_id Type: TEXT Description: Unique GDC identifier for this file (corresponds to the file_barcode)  --  this can be used to access more information from the GDC data portal like this: https://portal.gdc.cancer.gov/files/c21b332c-06c6-4403-9032-f91c8f407ba17
